<hr data-start=3D"2653" data-end=3D"2656">
<h3 data-section-id=3D"yyasah" data-start=3D"2658" data-end=3D"2680">5. AR =
Wearables =E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F</h3>
<p data-start=3D"2682" data-end=3D"2717">This depends heavily on the device=
.</p>
<p data-start=3D"2719" data-end=3D"2728">Examples:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2730" data-end=3D"2985">
<li data-section-id=3D"1l2icf5" data-start=3D"2730" data-end=3D"2812">
<p data-start=3D"2732" data-end=3D"2812">XREAL (formerly Nreal): some Andro=
id support that may require platform channels.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1n13zog" data-start=3D"2813" data-end=3D"2884">
<p data-start=3D"2815" data-end=3D"2884">Meta Quest: generally built with U=
nity or Unreal rather than Flutter.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"uga718" data-start=3D"2885" data-end=3D"2985">
<p data-start=3D"2887" data-end=3D"2985">Apple Vision Pro: native visionOS =
development is the primary approach; Flutter support is limited.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2987" data-end=3D"3105">Flutter can often serve as the sur=
rounding app, but immersive AR experiences on wearables usually rely on nat=
ive SDKs.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"3107" data-end=3D"3110">
<h2 data-section-id=3D"go0i9w" data-start=3D"3112" data-end=3D"3131">Flutte=
r packages</h2>
<p data-start=3D"3133" data-end=3D"3169">Some packages that can help includ=
e:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3171" data-end=3D"3351">
<li data-section-id=3D"1d0q4jw" data-start=3D"3171" data-end=3D"3221">
<p data-start=3D"3173" data-end=3D"3221"><code data-start=3D"3173" data-end=
=3D"3192">ar_flutter_plugin</code> (basic ARCore/ARKit support)</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"12w0muz" data-start=3D"3222" data-end=3D"3249">
<p data-start=3D"3224" data-end=3D"3249"><code data-start=3D"3224" data-end=
=3D"3238">arkit_plugin</code> (iOS only)</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"12bkmn5" data-start=3D"3250" data-end=3D"3267">
<p data-start=3D"3252" data-end=3D"3267"><code data-start=3D"3252" data-end=
=3D"3267">firebase_core</code></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"4nr03l" data-start=3D"3268" data-end=3D"3287">
<p data-start=3D"3270" data-end=3D"3287"><code data-start=3D"3270" data-end=
=3D"3287">cloud_firestore</code></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1x490qr" data-start=3D"3288" data-end=3D"3308">
<p data-start=3D"3290" data-end=3D"3308"><code data-start=3D"3290" data-end=
=3D"3308">firebase_storage</code></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"27lhbs" data-start=3D"3309" data-end=3D"3340">
<p data-start=3D"3311" data-end=3D"3340"><code data-start=3D"3311" data-end=
=3D"3326">google_ml_kit</code> (AI features)</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1yxh175" data-start=3D"3341" data-end=3D"3351">
<p data-start=3D"3343" data-end=3D"3351"><code data-start=3D"3343" data-end=
=3D"3351">camera</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"3353" data-end=3D"3628">Keep in mind that Flutter AR plugi=
ns sometimes lag behind the latest native SDK features. For advanced capabi=
lities like cloud anchors, geospatial APIs, or newer ARKit features, you ma=
y need to write native Android/iOS code and expose it to Flutter through pl=
atform channels.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"14lkt9b" data-start=3D"3630" data-end=3D"3652">Overa=
ll assessment</h3>
<p data-start=3D"3654" data-end=3D"4008">If your goal is a modern AR applic=
ation with features like collaborative sessions, cloud synchronization, per=
sistent objects, and AI-powered functionality, Flutter is a solid choice fo=
r the application layer. The main limitation is that you'll often rely on n=
ative AR SDKs underneath Flutter, especially for cutting-edge AR features a=
nd wearable support.</p>
<p data-start=3D"4010" data-end=3D"4314" data-is-last-node=3D"" data-is-onl=
y-node=3D"">If you're planning a production-grade AR app, I'd estimate Flut=
ter can comfortably handle <strong data-start=3D"4100" data-end=3D"4110">80=
=E2=80=9390%</strong> of the application (UI, networking, authentication, s=
tate management, backend integration), with the remaining <strong data-star=
t=3D"4222" data-end=3D"4232">10=E2=80=9320%</strong> involving native Andro=
id/iOS AR code for advanced platform-specific capabilities.</p></div></div>=
