<p data-start=3D"386" data-end=3D"412">If you fork it, you could:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"414" data-end=3D"779">
<li data-section-id=3D"zo52gv" data-start=3D"414" data-end=3D"463">
<p data-start=3D"416" data-end=3D"463">Update it to the latest Flutter embe=
dding APIs.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"psolht" data-start=3D"464" data-end=3D"511">
<p data-start=3D"466" data-end=3D"511">Migrate Android to newer ARCore SDK =
versions.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"tkaw29" data-start=3D"512" data-end=3D"574">
<p data-start=3D"514" data-end=3D"574">Update iOS to newer ARKit/RealityKit=
 APIs where appropriate.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"22ug9t" data-start=3D"575" data-end=3D"652">
<p data-start=3D"577" data-end=3D"652">Fix build issues as Android Gradle P=
lugin, Kotlin, Swift, and Xcode evolve.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"ojahjd" data-start=3D"653" data-end=3D"779">
<p data-start=3D"655" data-end=3D"779">Add features that the original plugi=
n never implemented (Cloud Anchors, Geospatial APIs, image tracking improve=
ments, etc.).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"781" data-end=3D"842">That has a few advantages over writi=
ng a plugin from scratch:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"844" data-end=3D"1078">
<li data-section-id=3D"1eatwm3" data-start=3D"844" data-end=3D"899">
<p data-start=3D"846" data-end=3D"899">You already have the platform channe=
l infrastructure.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"d6k9wl" data-start=3D"900" data-end=3D"935">
<p data-start=3D"902" data-end=3D"935">The Dart API is largely designed.</p=
>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"fd6qcr" data-start=3D"936" data-end=3D"1011">
<p data-start=3D"938" data-end=3D"1011">Scene management, node abstractions=
, and serialization are already there.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"q952wc" data-start=3D"1012" data-end=3D"1078">
<p data-start=3D"1014" data-end=3D"1078">Existing example apps can continue=
 to work with minimal changes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1080" data-end=3D"1294">The main challenge isn't Flutter i=
tself=E2=80=94it's keeping up with the native SDKs. ARCore and ARKit contin=
ue to evolve independently, so you'll need to maintain two native implement=
ations behind a common Dart interface.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"1ak92ae" data-start=3D"1296" data-end=3D"1324">Using=
 an AI coding agent</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1326" data-end=3D"1443">An AI coding agent like Antigravit=
y could be genuinely useful for this kind of work because much of it is rep=
etitive:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1445" data-end=3D"1628">
<li data-section-id=3D"1bmf7o1" data-start=3D"1445" data-end=3D"1480">
<p data-start=3D"1447" data-end=3D"1480">updating deprecated Android APIs,<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"vs3u2s" data-start=3D"1481" data-end=3D"1516">
<p data-start=3D"1483" data-end=3D"1516">migrating Gradle/Kotlin versions,<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"18160vb" data-start=3D"1517" data-end=3D"1545">
<p data-start=3D"1519" data-end=3D"1545">fixing Swift deprecations,</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1nc5vut" data-start=3D"1546" data-end=3D"1588">
<p data-start=3D"1548" data-end=3D"1588">generating platform channel boiler=
plate,</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"6h80m7" data-start=3D"1589" data-end=3D"1628">
<p data-start=3D"1591" data-end=3D"1628">keeping Android and iOS APIs align=
ed.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1630" data-end=3D"1858">The parts that still require caref=
ul engineering are the API design and testing. For example, deciding how a =
new ARCore feature should map into a cross-platform Dart API is a design de=
cision rather than a mechanical code change.</p>
