# Architectural Decisions

---

## Why SceneView?

Raw ARCore requires writing:

- renderer
- shaders
- PBR
- OpenGL
- GPU management

This is unnecessary.

SceneView already provides:

- Filament renderer
- Cube primitives
- GLB loading
- Active maintenance

---

## Why not Sceneform?

Deprecated.

No longer maintained.

---

## Why not OpenGL directly?

Writing a renderer is outside the scope of the project.

We are building an AR engine.

Not a game engine.

---

## Why not Unity?

Too heavy.

Too coupled.

Requires Unity ecosystem.

---

## Why Platform Channels?

ARCore is native.

MethodChannel provides:

- clean abstraction
- no C bindings
- maintainable architecture

---

## Why Platform Views?

ARCore requires a native rendering surface.

Hybrid Composition is currently the best approach.

---

