# Rules for Future Development

## Never

- expose ARCore classes
- expose ARKit classes
- expose SceneView classes
- expose RealityKit classes
- let Flutter perform hit tests
- let Flutter manage anchors
- let Flutter know renderer implementation
- write custom rendering unless absolutely necessary
- introduce abstractions for hypothetical features

---

## Always

- keep Flutter platform-agnostic
- keep rendering native
- build one subsystem at a time
- prefer composition over inheritance
- separate responsibilities
- document architectural decisions
- keep APIs minimal
- optimize for long-term maintainability

